      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/michaelkernaghan/contextuality/tree/ea5d9972a2e29b23cedfb4bd31446ad761aedd52",
        "note": "Lean code for the paper \"The Algebraic Landscape of Kochen-Specker Sets in Dimension Three\" (arXiv:2603.16988; the repository's current version is 11, and versions 1-9 are withdrawn). Its lean/ project (Mathlib) proves that named ray sets in C^3 admit no Kochen-Specker colouring (KSNamed, KSCyclotomic.cabello_S6_uncolorable), minimum sizes of such sets in coordinate pools (KSMin.PeresPool.minimum_33, KSMin.IntPool.minimum_31), and KSCyclotomic.six_divides_iff_ks_uncolorable: the pool of 0 and the n-th roots of unity is uncolourable exactly when 6 divides n. With its monotonicity lemma these give the colouring form in C^3 for those sets. Its lean-ks/ project (core Lean) checks uncolourability certificates for Peres's 33 and Conway and Kochen's 31 at the level of labels. The checker here (KochenSpecker/Checker.lean) uses the same method, a case-split tree over a list-based partial assignment checked with decide, which the author read in lean-ks/ before writing it; it was written separately (explicit pair and triad lists, a single conflict-detecting leaf, exactly-one triads) and no file was copied. The repository states no open-source licence.",
